# Avatar's Wrath, cast with no target, airbends every creature (CR 701.65a): Bot1's Giver of Runes, Bot2's Snapcaster Mage
# and Bot2's two Spirit tokens, which cease to exist in exile (CR 111.7). The Wrath exiles itself as its last instruction.
# "Until your next turn, your opponents can't cast spells from anywhere other than their hands" (CR 101.2, 611.2c):
# - Bot1 is not an opponent of itself: it casts its own airbended Giver of Runes from exile for {2} at once.
# - In Bot2's turn 8, with the mana for both, neither the airbended Snapcaster Mage (from exile, for {2}) nor Lingering
#   Souls' flashback (from the graveyard) is offered, still not in its end step; Ornithopter from its hand is cast.
# - The effect ends as Bot1's turn 9 begins (CR 611.2b): in Bot1's upkeep Bot2 casts the flash Snapcaster from exile for
#   {2}, and in turn 10 flashes back Lingering Souls - the positive controls for both refusals.

